  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In the given cycle, heat is supplied in process $D$ to $A$ at constant volume and in process $A$ to $B$ at constant pressure.\n$\\therefore$ Heat supplied, $Q=n C_V(\\Delta T)_{D A}+n C_p(\\Delta T)_{A B}$\nFor an ideal monoatomic gas,\n$\\begin{aligned}\nC_V & =\\frac{3}{2} R \\text { and } C_p=\\frac{5}{2} R \\\\\n\\Rightarrow \\quad Q & =\\frac{3}{2} n R \\Delta T+\\frac{5}{2} n R \\Delta T \\quad[\\because n R \\Delta T=p \\Delta V] \\\\\n& =\\frac{3}{2}\\left(p_0 V_0\\right)+5\\left(p_0 V_0\\right) \\\\\n& =\\frac{13}{2} p_0 V_0\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
